From: hashtagbasit
Subject: drm/panel: vtdr6130-cog: select the page before the RP6 frame length

The Retroid Pocket 6 init sequence sent "AA 10" without the F0 page select
command in front, so the panel never switched to page 0x10 and the B1
frame length write that follows went to the wrong page: the panel ran on
its reset frame length instead of the one meant for 60 and 120 Hz. Send it
as F0 AA 10 like every other page switch here (ROCKNIX fixed the same line
in their RP6 panel patch).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-visionox-vtdr6130-cog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-visionox-vtdr6130-cog.c
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
 					0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00);
 	}
 
-	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xAA, 0x10);
+	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xF0, 0xAA, 0x10);
 
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xB1, 
 				0x02, 0x16, 0x00, 0x14, 0x00, 0x1C, 0x00, 0x02,
